uml-nt: io_uring defaults OFF under OS_WINDOWS

The M5.1c net-gate crash hunt caught the io_uring task-exit path
smashing task stacks (kernel runs 36710288173 / 36711876142 /
36714161309 on the diag commits 88459b7..120a649). Nothing in this
port creates an io_uring ring — busybox/udhcpc never touch it and
copy_process zeroes p->io_uring (kernel/fork.c) — yet EVERY dying
task runs do_exit -> io_uring_files_cancel (kernel/exit.c) ->
__io_uring_cancel_generic -> io_uring_clean_tctx ->
io_uring_del_tctx_node.

On a task whose ->io_uring holds stale memory, that chain
list_del's and kfree's through FREED STACK vmalloc memory:
list_del(&node->ctx_node) writes through stale stack values into
live task stacks (the forgiving pad guard caught rip=6001d362
writing the pad pages of four different stacks), and
kfree(node)/kfree(tctx) feed vmalloc-stack addresses into the SLUB
freelist — later kmallocs hand freed stack memory out as slab
objects and slab writes spray the 0/1-byte arrays over suspended
tasks' schedule chains (the ~0x210-byte smash, pad qword ->
0x1000000) that killed the net reader (ret to 0x1000100, DEP-X) the
moment the vector channel went live.

No guest user needs io_uring, so the subsystem must not even be
built. Make the base default OS_WINDOWS-conditional instead of
forcing "# CONFIG_IO_URING is not set" through the defconfig:
kconfig silently drops that line for an EXPERT-hidden symbol
without CONFIG_EXPERT=y, and CONFIG_EXPERT=y flips a dozen
default-y-if-!EXPERT knobs (BINFMT_SCRIPT, SHMEM, EPOLL, ...) the
port relies on.

Under OS_LINUX (plain UML, the lts CI recipe) the default stays y —
untouched.

Signed-off-by: quangdz-comeback <204571370+quangdz-comeback@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 init/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/Kconfig b/init/Kconfig
--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -1837,7 +1837,12 @@ config AIO
 config IO_URING
 	bool "Enable IO uring support" if EXPERT
 	select IO_WQ
-	default y
+	# uml-nt: the exit path (io_uring_files_cancel -> clean_tctx ->
+	# del_tctx_node) runs for every dying task; with no ring user,
+	# a stale ->io_uring there walks freed stack memory and sprays
+	# the SLUB freelist with vmalloc-stack addresses (the M5.1c
+	# stack smash). Default OFF for the NT port.
+	default y if !OS_WINDOWS
 	help
 	  This option enables support for the io_uring interface, enabling
 	  applications to submit and complete IO through submission and
